statement:
Let N, n ∈ ℕ, ι a finite nonempty index type, and μ a measure on E := ℝ^N, evaluated on arbitrary sets as an outer measure. Let A ⊆ E, δ ∈ ℝ, κ > 0 and a ∈ E. Let X : ℝ → 𝒫(E) and Z : ι → ℝ → 𝒫(E) be families of sets, Ax a proposition and (Ax′_j)_{j∈ι} propositions. Write B(a, r) for the open ball and ofReal := ENNReal.ofReal. Assume:
(i) Z_j(s) ⊆ X(s) for every j and every s > 0;
(ii) X(s) ⊆ ⋃_j Z_j(κs) for every s > 0;
(iii) Ax′_j implies Ax for every j;
(iv) for every j, Ψ0_j ∨ Ψ∞_j ∨ Ax′_j, where
 Ψ0_j: for every c > 0 there is ε > 0 with μ(A ∩ (Z_j(s) ∩ B(a, r))) ≤ ofReal(c(rs)ⁿ) for all 0 < s < ε and 0 < r < δ;
 Ψ∞_j: for every K ∈ ℝ and ε > 0 there are 0 < s < ε and 0 < r < δ with ofReal(K(rs)ⁿ) ≤ μ(A ∩ (Z_j(s) ∩ B(a, r))).
Then Φ0 ∨ Φ∞ ∨ Ax, where Φ0 and Φ∞ are Ψ0_j and Ψ∞_j with X(s) in place of Z_j(s).
